ersion":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":69771,"output_tokens":2322,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"17ed22fc97dfa8d93f513f545f32c33b4d49d81fbfbb3516f83bdef55f976c14"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":281201,"output_tokens":4418,"requests":18}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"12c41971c2488ef4cd89f8ab2a89d502c5c4a9f2986f817ee26b2d80e0b4647c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":47311,"output_tokens":1823,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3c3a108459b5bb8ecb32c0784d38a52b747b9a754eef2ccae16724d4a985b30d"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":238484,"output_tokens":6009,"requests":15}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify whether batch_sink wraps _finalize_claims per successful item or the whole lease-bounded loop, and explicitly scope the stale-path _queue.enqueue (line 499) and _record_item_failure writes as included-in / excluded-from the finalize batch.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_finalize_claims iterates `for tid, snap, result, exc in results` where results come from a `_lease_bounded_batch(cfg)` batch (drain(): line 313-318)","Stale path calls `_queue.enqueue(tid, soak_min=0, repo_root=repo_root)` at enrich_drain.py:499, which also routes through _seam.append_event and would enter an active batch_sink","AC5 states finalize collapses to 'CLAIM + batched-finalize (2 commits)', framed around a single successful item, but a multi-item batch or a concurrent stale re-enqueue would put more events into the finalize commit"],"finding":"The plan's mechanism wraps _finalize_claims in a batch_sink, but that function loops over a lease-bounded batch (potentially >1 item) and, on the stale-drift path, also calls _queue.enqueue(tid, soak_min=0) (enrich_drain.py:499) plus _record_item_failure dispositions — writes that also route through the same _seam.append_event and would be swept into the same commit. The plan describes only the single-item TICKET_DIGEST+DONE_ENRICH pair and does not enumerate these additional in-scope writes or state whether the sink wraps per-item or the whole loop.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f67c3b93c948a21e8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan / Mechanism step 1; Worked example; AC5","norm_id":"n8a5263d26658fd40","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A drain batch of 2+ soaked tickets runs one drain; the AC5 'exactly two commits' fixture may not describe multi-item behavior","One item drifts during its enrich window: its ENQUEUE_ENRICH re-enqueue joins the same finalize commit as other items' DIGEST+DONE"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Clarify in Mechanism step 1 that the sink spans the full _finalize_claims loop and that all events it buffers (including any stale-drift ENQUEUE_ENRICH re-enqueues and failure dispositions) flush in one commit; adjust AC5/worked example to describe the multi-item batch case, or scope the fixture to single-item and note multi-item behavior explicitly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverif